    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Canopy reflectance spectra were measured under variable sky conditions with a SVC HR-1024i Spectroradiometer with an 8-degree field-of-view (FOV) foreoptic lens. The reflectance type is indicated in the data. Relative reflectance is the reflectance is calculated as the ratio of the radiance or DN of the target (e.g. leaf, canopy, soil) divided by the radiance or DN of the Spectralon standard for each instrument channel. Spectralon_corrected reflectance, the reflectance is calculated as the ratio of the radiance or DN of the target (e.g. leaf, canopy, soil) divided by the radiance or DN of the Spectralon standard for each instrument channel and then multiplied by the spectral response of the Spectralon standard.Data were processed using a combination of R-FieldSpectra (Serbin, 2021) and spectrolab (Meireles & Schweiger, 2020), available from https://github.com/serbinsh/R-FieldSpectra and https://github.com/meireles/spectrolab respectively.",
      "dGPS data were collected using a Trimble Geo 7X (H-Star) handheld device and data were processed according to manufacturer?s instructions (https://geospatial.trimble.com).Explanation of dGPS processing results and correction codes:Dilution of precision (Max_PDOP, Max_HDOP)A specification of error propagation on measurement precision due to satellite geometry. For further information see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dilution_of_precision_(navigation). For a description of the different correction types, please refer to the Standard Processing Types and code descriptions provided in Exercise 5.3: Create your own GIS export setup and Glossary sections of the Trimble ORIENTATION GUIDE TerraSync Software and GPS Pathfinder\u00ae Office Software ( https://www.neigps.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/TS_PFO_Orientation_Guide_v70a_201205092.pdf).",
      "Methods References Jose Eduardo Meireles, & Anna Schweiger. (2020, July 7). meireles/spectrolab: CRAN-v0.0.9 (Version CRAN-v0.0.9). Zenodo. http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3934575Shawn P. Serbin. (2021, February 18). serbinsh/R-FieldSpectra: Update license and docs (Version v0.9.6). Zenodo. http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4548961"
    ],
